		shortDescription: "Subtracting vectors by reversing the subtrahend and adding: $\\vec{A} - \\vec{B} = \\vec{A} + (-\\vec{B})$.",
		conceptIntro: "Vector subtraction measures the change or difference between two vector states. It is defined directly through vector addition by adding the negative (reversed) vector.",
		physicalInterpretation: "Average acceleration depends on $\\Delta \\vec{v} = \\vec{v}_f - \\vec{v}_i$. Even if a car maintains constant speed around a turn, $\\vec{v}_f - \\vec{v}_i$ is non-zero because the direction changed!",
