		physicalInterpretation: "Notice the subtle distinction: the definite integral $\\int_{t_1}^{t_2} a(t)\\,dt$ equals the CHANGE in velocity $\\Delta v = v(t_2) - v(t_1)$, which equals the signed area under the $a$–$t$ curve. Even if $a(t)$ smoothly ramps up or oscillates, the integral accumulates every tiny impulse of acceleration cleanly.",
